		{
			"id":"1970226e2cb4f746",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Maintenance\n## Writing\n- Track Changes: accept/reject suggestions\n- Screen Garden: Google Docs style collaboration, fine tuned permissions -> scheduled to be open by Sept. 26, but no update yet\n- Vault CMS: easily bulk update properties\n- Citations: \n- Templater: \n- Speech Kit: speech-to-text\n- Handwriting: enter handwritten text in blocks from pen inputs\n- \n\n## Import, Export, Sharing\n- Share Note\n- Pandoc\n- \n## Behind the Scenes\n- Dataview: still supports more queries than Bases\n- Tag Wrangler: \n- ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":40,
			"y":-328,
			"width":380,
			"height":600
		},
		{
			"id":"b245af463a03a886",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# UX\n\n## Interface Navigation\n- Omnisearch: search text within notes, results are still unusually messy and unprioritized\n\n## Homepage\n- Apex Dashboard: classes, projects, calendar, Pomodoro timer\n- Vault Logo: upload ADVANCE logo to all vaults\n\n## Division between notes/sections\n- Longform: allows manually setting order of files within a \"project\"\n- Breadcrumbs: different relationships between notes by classes in metadata, can be slow, displays in dedicated side-bar which I don't really love.\n## Appearance\n- Unseen Changes Dot: marks files that have been updated, might be nice to let students/centers see, especially for documentation\n- Cornell Marginalia: add marginal notes, great; but makes cursor freak out with arrow key use (Heather didn't have this problem)\n",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1630,
			"y":-328,
			"width":420,
			"height":600
		},
		{"id":"885c809d3326a67b","type":"text","text":"# Teaching\n## Content\n\n\n\n## Assignments\n- Quizzes:\n\t- Quizzable\n\t- CBT-Exam: smart review, score history, flagged for review\n\t- LearnKit: spaced-repetition, flashcards, tests\n- Maps:\n\t- Maps\n\t- Leaflet\n\t- Map View\n- Family Trees:\n\t- Charted Roots: bridge tree to map movements, timeline creation\n\t- Grafily: simpler\n\n- Story Line: maps, graphs, objectives, resources, lots of stuff\n\n## Biblical Language Tools\n- Torah Verse Inserter: inserts in textblock, Aleppo Codex text via Sefaria, \n- Diacritics-Free Search: I think this feature got added in a recent update for all Obsidian\n- YouVersion Linker: \n- The Scripture Injector: inserts as callout, supports ESV if you input your own free API key\n- RTL Support: sets notes to RTL/LTR; also possibly replaced by general update\n- Wordbook Layout: ??, for vocab\n- Makarios: \"smart book mapper\"?, auto-complete verse references, side-by-side Bible versions\n- Bible Search: translations, cross-references, maps, church history family tree\n- Blur: hide text, reveal on mouse-over\n- ","x":-780,"y":-328,"width":400,"height":600},
		{
			"id":"1b4fbd413c2c2799",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Design",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1170,
			"y":-328,
			"width":360,
			"height":600
		},
		{
			"id":"18d4395c108d6514",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Future Questions\n- Standardized treatment of the relationships between units\n\t- Relationship Indicators: folder, type, subtype, tag, link\n\t- Magnitude: book, chapter, note, summary, header, section, tip\n\t- File Type: text, image, video, slideshow, audio\n\t- Task: reading, lecture, assignment, assessment, discussion\n\t- Visual Layout: horizontal, vertical, embedded, hidden/reveal, sequential\n\t- \n1. ",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-810,
			"y":480,
			"width":620,
			"height":540
		},
		{
			"id":"80075620b607cff6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Write-up\nThe system will change we design, teach, and improve educational experiences through promoting increased efficiency, quality, and transparency.\n\n### Rationale of Paths & Ends\nThe system has multiple, worthy ends and, in order to make use as easy as possible, allows multiple paths to accomplish those ends. Each additional path makes the system easier because it reduces constraints but adds complexity. To maximize the value of each path, every designed path has a unique start and end location. Effectively, there are 2 kinds of paths: main paths and short-cuts. Main paths begin from a centralized location and are clearly oriented around key tasks. Short-cuts move between end or intermediate stages and are useful when completing related, sequential tasks, or when completing an unexpected task.\nTo maximize simplicity, the main path is always described in the instructions. Short-cuts are (a) only included when they address a closely related, non-obvious, and sequential tasks and (b) located in a call-out (collapsed?) for easy visual separation (Does this draw attention where it doesn't need to be?)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":0,
			"y":480,
			"width":460,
			"height":600
		},
		{
			"id":"5106a9645759a150",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Software & Pricing Trade-offs\nIn order to continue to offer reduced pricing and increased software support, ADVANCE requests the follow 3 things from Centers:\n- (-) perform any remaining manual data entry tasks\n- (+) try to improve at least 1 thing about your center\n- (+) use some of the time and money you save for Jesus",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-1580,
			"y":920,
			"width":480,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"80758ccde7f6226a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Design Principles\n1. **Functionality Over Familiarity**\n2. **Proprietary In, Open Out**\n3. **1 Source, Many Derivatives**\n4. **High Structure, Low Constraints**\n5. **1 Process, Many Resources**\n6. **Layered Optionality for Zombies & Rebels**",
			"styleAttributes":{
				"textAlign":"center",
				"shape":null
			},
			"x":-1300,
			"y":-1550,
			"width":380,
			"height":260,
			"color":"6"
		},
		{
			"id":"2315e12a547fd062",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"# Core Values\n1. **Accessible**\n\t- language\n\t- ease of use\n\t- familiarity\n\t- tech support\n\t- flexibility\n\t- mouse & keyboard support\n\t- hardware sensitive (light)\n2. **Comprehensive**\n\t- wide swath of features integrated into 1 tool\n\t- incorporate as many parts of the educational process as possible\n\t- accommodate all use cases\n3. **Helpful**\n\t- efficiency\n\t- improvement\n\t- innovation\n\t- transparency\n4. **Scaleable**\n\t- single structure\n\t- fixed costs only (no per user, per use)\n\t- low tech maintenance skills\n\t- distributed oversight",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-360,
			"y":-1510,
			"width":240,
			"height":220,
			"color":"6"
		}
	],
